## How to use this template

This file is the **producer side** of the cross-repo memory protocol.

1. Fork to root of any repo as `RUBY_BRIEF.md`.
2. Update `last_updated` frontmatter with `date -u +"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ"` (UTC ISO-8601 with Z, NEVER local time, NEVER numeric offset).
3. After each meaningful session, append to "Material Changes Since Last Brief" + bump `last_updated`.
4. Run `accio!` ritual which updates this file + commits.
5. Consumer side (ruby-assistant or equivalent strategic-memory folder) pulls via `sync!` and applies updates.

See `docs/02-cross-repo-memory.md` (planned) for full protocol.

This pattern adapted from running 8+ ventures under one holding. See parent `claude-code-kit` repo for context.
